  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Labels are our judgment of how far income and reach can grow, not a ranking of difficulty. The work descriptions are general practice knowledge. Demand signals come from Mint, which reported in 2026 that a large firm saw corporate law as one of its most active hiring segments, followed by banking and finance (<a href="https://www.livemint.com/industry/law-firms-buck-india-inc-slowdown-with-double-digit-salary-hikes-promotions-11780806196488.html" rel="noopener">Mint, 8 June 2026</a>).
  </p>

  <h2 id="route-verdict">Firm, in-house, boutique: the verdict by route</h2>

  <p>
    The same degree leads to six corporate routes with different gates. Routes you can sell directly come first; salaried ladders follow with their risk named.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
