          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>Why compliance advisory and the boutique lead.</strong> Both sell a skill to many clients. You set the price, you can add packages or juniors, and a repeat client costs less to win than a new one. A salaried associate or in-house post, however respected, moves up a set pay ladder with a narrow top.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Skill portfolio first.</strong> In every row the strongest outcomes pair one core skill (drafting or a regulation), one multiplier (a sector, finance sense or AI use) and proof another person can check.
    </p>
  </div>

