      <ul>
        {aiLater.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="boutique">Building a boutique business layer</h2>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>This is the ownership path in corporate law.</strong> A boutique, or independent counsel, scales because you set the fee, you can package repeat work, you can add juniors or part-time associates, and returning clients and referrals reduce the cost of finding the next one. Firm ladders cap at a pay band. A practice with a niche and repeat clients does not.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    The money layer in corporate law is basic and rarely taught. Learn this version early.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Route</th>
          <th>Who pays</th>
          <th>How they find and trust you</th>
          <th>First skill to learn</th>
          <th>One number to watch</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {moneyRows.map((item) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Route"><strong>{item.route}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Who pays">{item.pays}</td>
