            <td data-label="First skill to learn">{item.skill}</td>
            <td data-label="One number to watch">{item.number}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Clear English, written and spoken, moves every row of that table, because clients and partners judge you first by how plainly you explain. A boutique needs a few habits: one narrow niche, a clear written scope and fee for each engagement, a deposit on larger work, and a checklist for every repeat task so someone else can do it later. Check current GST and registration rules for professional services on the official portals before you invoice.
  </p>

  <p>
    Advocates cannot advertise or solicit work, and a full-time salaried job ends the right to practise in court. Read the rules in the <a href="/blog/career-options/law-career-options/">law career options guide</a> and ask your State Bar Council before any publicity step. Advisory and company-side work that is not court practice may differ, so confirm your own case. This is why referrals from accountants, company secretaries and former colleagues matter so much. Employer-only routes, such as a firm associate post, need this sales layer mainly for the move after it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="add-ons">Company secretary and LLM add-ons</h2>

  <p>
    Add-ons help only when they close one named gap. Match each to the route, and judge it against your budget: roughly 10 percent of the total education budget as a starting benchmark, and a serious caution near 20 percent.
